-- OWNERSHIP fixture for rule-stdlib-reimpl (#2248 Miss 1, S-ownership-exemption).
-- This fixture's own file id is `list` (`modIdOf` = basename minus `.mdk`), the
-- same module id the real stdlib uses for `list.reverse`. Before this slice the
-- rule had no ownership concept at all: any file whose path did not literally
-- contain a "stdlib" path segment (this one doesn't -- it lives under
-- test/lint_fixtures/) fired on ANY name+signature match, so this exact
-- `reverse` would have been a false positive. Ownership (the linted file's own
-- module == the matched candidate's module) must suppress it -- the true
-- owner's canonical definition is never a "reimplementation" of itself.
export
reverse : List a -> List a
reverse [] = []
reverse (x::xs) = reverse xs ++ [x]
